  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: Transformer aggregation clearly outperforms avgpool (+5.6% accuracy: 0.6878 vs 0.6315) with the same scvi_n200/resnet50/concat setup, making transformer the proven aggregation choice. The largest unexplored architectural variable is the image encoder: resnet50 is a relatively modest CNN, while imagenet_vit_l (ViT-Large) offers substantially richer visual representations. This experiment (config_028) isolates the image-encoder upgrade by keeping all other settings identical to the current best (config_018: scvi_n200, transformer, concat, multiprofile), so any accuracy change can be attributed to the image encoder. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, testing the highest-impact unexplored dimension (image representation quality) is more informative than a small fusion-method tweak (concat→weighted). If ViT-L delivers a meaningful gain, subsequent experiments can layer in weighted fusion or scgpt on top. Expected cost: ViT-L is considerably larger than ResNet50, so I estimate ~9–12 GPU hours (roughly 2× the 5.16 h of config_018), but the potential accuracy uplift justifies the higher compute spend relative to a marginal fusion change."
}

